{% comment %}
  Agenda - the day as a list, with the gaps between things marked.

  A list of meetings is not a day. The holes are half of it: three meetings
  back to back and three spread over eight hours are the same list and
  completely different afternoons, and the only difference on screen is whether
  anything says so. So the empty stretches are drawn as entries in their own
  right.

  How many rows fit is arithmetic on the box, not a number per size: at four
  rows the list holds two meetings and at twelve it holds eight, and the entry
  that will not fit is counted rather than clipped.
{% endcomment %}

{%- assign day = calendar -%}
{%- assign hh = "now" | date: "%H" | times: 60 -%}
{%- assign now_mins = "now" | date: "%M" | plus: hh -%}

{%- comment %} How many are actually left, counted against the clock at the
  moment of drawing rather than taken from the payload. `today.remaining` was
  true when Google was last asked, which is up to ten minutes ago, and this
  design decides what to *say* from the live clock - so the two disagree for
  the whole of that window and the panel prints "6 left" beside "Nothing left
  today". Same reason the countdowns are worked out here. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign left = 0 -%}
{%- for event in day.events -%}
  {%- if event.end_minutes > now_mins %}{% assign left = left | plus: 1 %}{% endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
{%- assign gone = day.today.total | minus: left | at_least: 0 -%}

{%- assign box_w = shape.width | at_least: 160 -%}
{%- assign box_h = shape.height | at_least: 140 -%}
{%- assign pad = box_w | divided_by: 24 | at_least: 10 | at_most: 22 -%}

{%- comment %} Everything still to come, plus what is already done when the
  widget was told to keep it - which is the setting for a wall somebody walks
  past all day, where a day that empties itself reads as a broken screen. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign shown = day.upcoming -%}
{%- if extension.values.show_done %}{% assign shown = day.events %}{% endif -%}

{%- assign located = false -%}
{%- if extension.values.show_location != false and box_w > 240 %}{% assign located = true %}{% endif -%}

{%- assign row_h = 34 -%}
{%- if located %}{% assign row_h = 48 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if box_h < 220 %}{% assign row_h = 30 %}{% endif -%}

{%- assign header = 46 -%}
{%- if day.all_day.size > 0 and box_h > 200 %}{% assign header = header | plus: 28 %}{% endif -%}
{%- if notices.size > 0 %}{% assign header = header | plus: 34 %}{% endif -%}
{%- comment %} Floored, or the count of what did not fit is a fraction. The
  panel is 800 by 480 and a three-column box is 200 wide, so `pad` comes out of
  a division that is not exact - and one float anywhere in this chain reaches
  the screen as "+2.5333333333333 more", which reads as a broken widget rather
  than as a full list. {% endcomment -%}
{%- assign slots = box_h | minus: header | minus: pad | divided_by: row_h | floor | at_least: 1 | at_most: 9 -%}
{%- assign hidden = shown | size | minus: slots -%}

<div class="screen{% if box_w < 260 %} dense{% endif %}">
  <div class="title-bar" style="padding: {{ pad }}px {{ pad }}px 8px">
    <div class="title" style="font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 18 | at_least: 16 | at_most: 30 }}px">
      {{ extension.values.heading | default: "Today" }}
    </div>
    {%- comment %} "0 left" is arithmetic rather than news. A day that is over
      says so, and a day that never had anything says that instead. {% endcomment -%}
    {% if box_w > 210 %}
      <div class="chip">
        <span class="i i-calendar"></span>
        {% if left > 0 %}{{ left }} left
        {% elsif day.today.total > 0 %}all done
        {% else %}clear{% endif %}
      </div>
    {% else %}
      <div class="t-sm t-bold">
        {% if left > 0 %}{{ left }}{% else %}&check;{% endif %}
      </div>
    {% endif %}
  </div>

  {% if day.all_day.size > 0 and box_h > 200 %}
    <div style="border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 5px {{ pad }}px">
      <p class="with-icon t-xs truncate" style="gap: 6px">
        <span class="i i-calendar-check i-xs"></span>
        <span class="truncate t-bold">{% for entry in day.all_day %}{{ entry.title }}{% unless forloop.last %} &middot; {% endunless %}{% endfor %}</span>
      </p>
    </div>
  {% endif %}

  {%- if shown.size == 0 -%}
    {%- comment %} An empty list is still a list design, so it draws one.

      A centred "Nothing left today" is the correct fact and the least useful
      picture on the panel: it is what the screen shows from six o'clock until
      midnight every day, and it says nothing a person crossing the room wanted
      to know. What they wanted is what is coming, and the days that were
      fetched already carry it - a count, a first time and how much of each day
      is spoken for. Drawn as bars, that is a week at a glance.

      Only the days that were actually asked for, though. "The rest of today"
      fetches one day, and seven empty bars under it would be an invented
      week - so a one-day window draws the day that has just gone instead,
      which is a thing this widget does know. {% endcomment -%}
    {%- assign ahead = day.days | size -%}
    {%- assign peak = 60 -%}
    {%- for entry in day.days -%}
      {%- if entry.busy_minutes > peak %}{% assign peak = entry.busy_minutes %}{% endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- comment %} The rows share out the height rather than sitting at a fixed
      one: six days stacked 26 pixels tall at the top of a twelve-row box is a
      list that looks like it stopped loading. Bounded either side, so two days
      are not drawn as two bands and nine are still legible. {% endcomment -%}
    {%- assign day_count = day.days.size | minus: 1 | at_least: 1 -%}
    {%- assign room = box_h | minus: header | minus: pad | minus: 34 | at_least: 40 -%}
    {%- assign day_row = room | divided_by: day_count | floor | at_least: 20 | at_most: 46 -%}
    {%- assign day_slots = room | divided_by: day_row | floor | at_least: 1 | at_most: 9 -%}

    <div class="content" style="padding: 6px {{ pad }}px {{ pad }}px">
      <div class="layout layout--col" style="gap: 6px">
        {%- comment %} `empty_label` is about the whole window - "Nothing this
          week" - and printing it over a list of what is on this week is a
          screen arguing with itself. It is only the true sentence when there
          is nothing anywhere ahead. Something still to come *today* but past a
          short horizon is neither case, and `empty_label` is right there too:
          for a rolling window it says how many hours it looked at. {% endcomment -%}
        {%- assign said = day.empty_label | default: "Nothing left today" -%}
        {%- if day.next_any and day.next_any_day != "Today" %}{% assign said = "Nothing left today" %}{% endif -%}
        <p class="with-icon t-bold truncate" style="flex: none; gap: 6px">
          <span class="i i-calendar-check i-sm"></span>
          <span class="truncate">{{ said }}</span>
        </p>

        {% if ahead > 1 %}
          <div class="fit" style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 0; overflow: hidden">
            {% for entry in day.days offset: 1 limit: day_slots %}
              {%- assign width = entry.busy_minutes | times: 100 | divided_by: peak -%}
              <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; flex: none;
                          box-sizing: border-box; height: {{ day_row }}px;
                          border-top: 1px solid var(--ink)">
                <span class="t-xs t-bold" style="flex: none; width: {% if box_w > 260 %}30{% else %}22{% endif %}px">
                  {% if box_w > 260 %}{{ entry.day }}{% else %}{{ entry.day | slice: 0, 1 }}{% endif %}
                </span>

                {%- comment %} A day with nothing on it is an outlined box
                  rather than no box, or a clear Saturday reads as a row that
                  failed to draw. {% endcomment -%}
                <div class="fit" style="height: 11px; border: 2px solid var(--ink)">
                  {% if entry.busy_minutes > 0 %}
                    <div style="height: 100%; width: {{ width | at_least: 4 }}%;
                                {% if entry.is_weekend %}background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--ink) 0 3px, var(--paper) 3px 6px){% else %}background: var(--ink){% endif %}"></div>
                  {% endif %}
                </div>

                <span class="t-xs" style="flex: none; white-space: nowrap">
                  {% if entry.count > 0 %}{{ entry.count }} &middot; {{ entry.first }}{% else %}clear{% endif %}
                </span>
              </div>
            {% endfor %}
          </div>
        {% else %}
          {%- comment %} One day was asked for and it is over. The day that has
            just gone, hatched because every part of it is behind you. {% endcomment -%}
          <div class="fit layout layout--col layout--center" style="gap: 8px">
            {% if day.today.total > 0 %}
              <div style="flex: none; width: 100%">
                {%- assign open = day.window.open -%}
                {%- assign span = day.window.span | at_least: 120 -%}
                <div style="position: relative; border: 2px solid var(--ink); width: 100%;
                            height: {{ box_h | divided_by: 10 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 24 }}px">
                  {% for event in day.events %}
                    {%- assign from = event.start_minutes | minus: open -%}
                    {%- assign until = event.end_minutes | minus: open -%}
                    {%- if until > 0 and from < span -%}
                      {%- if from < 0 %}{% assign from = 0 %}{% endif -%}
                      {%- if until > span %}{% assign until = span %}{% endif -%}
                      {%- assign at = from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
                      {%- assign wide = until | minus: from | times: 1000 | divided_by: span -%}
                      <span style="position: absolute; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: {{ at | divided_by: 10.0 }}%;
                                   width: {{ wide | divided_by: 10.0 }}%; min-width: 3px;
                                   background: repeating-linear-gradient(45deg, var(--ink) 0 2px, var(--paper) 2px 5px)"></span>
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {% endfor %}
                </div>
                <p class="t-xs t-center" style="margin-top: 5px">
                  {{ day.today.total }} today, {{ day.today.busy_text }} of it{% if day.today.last_end != blank %}, done by {{ day.today.last_end }}{% endif %}
                </p>
              </div>
            {% else %}
              <p class="t-sm t-center">Nothing on it at all.</p>
            {% endif %}
          </div>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    <div class="content content--tight" style="padding: 6px {{ pad }}px">
      <div class="timeline">
        {%- assign edge = 0 -%}
        {% for event in shown limit: slots %}
          {%- comment %} The hole between the last thing and this one, when it
            is long enough to be worth crossing a room for. `edge` is where the
            day had got to; before the first entry it is now. {% endcomment -%}
          {%- if forloop.first -%}
            {%- assign edge = now_mins -%}
            {%- if event.start_minutes < edge %}{% assign edge = event.start_minutes %}{% endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
          {%- assign hole = event.start_minutes | minus: edge -%}

          {% if extension.values.show_gaps != false and hole >= 25 and box_h > 190 %}
            <div class="entry" style="padding: 2px 0">
              <span class="at t-xs" style="font-weight: 400">{{ hole | span_in_words }}</span>
              <span class="spine">
                <span style="border-left: 2px dashed var(--ink); flex: 1; width: 0"></span>
              </span>
              <span class="t-xs" style="align-self: center">free</span>
            </div>
          {% endif %}

          {%- assign until = event.start_minutes | minus: now_mins -%}
          {%- assign running = false -%}
          {%- if until <= 0 and event.end_minutes > now_mins %}{% assign running = true %}{% endif -%}
          {%- assign done = false -%}
          {%- if event.end_minutes <= now_mins %}{% assign done = true %}{% endif -%}

          <div class="entry" style="padding: {{ row_h | minus: 26 | divided_by: 2 | at_least: 2 }}px 0">
            <span class="at" style="font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 26 | at_least: 12 | at_most: 17 }}px{% if done %}; text-decoration: line-through{% endif %}">
              {% if event.start_minutes >= 1440 %}+{{ event.start }}{% else %}{{ event.start }}{% endif %}
            </span>
            <span class="spine">
              <span class="node{% if running %} node--now{% endif %}"></span>
            </span>
            <span class="body">
              <span class="what truncate" style="display: block; font-size: {{ box_w | divided_by: 24 | at_least: 13 | at_most: 19 }}px{% if done %}; text-decoration: line-through{% endif %}">
                {{ event.title }}
              </span>
              {% if located and event.location != blank %}
                <span class="where">
                  <span class="i i-{% if event.remote %}video{% else %}pin{% endif %} i-xs"></span>
                  <span class="truncate">{{ event.location }}</span>
                  {% if event.conflict %}<span class="i i-alert i-xs"></span>{% endif %}
                </span>
              {% elsif running %}
                <span class="where"><span class="i i-dot i-xs"></span>on now</span>
              {% endif %}
            </span>
          </div>

          {%- assign edge = event.end_minutes -%}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>

      {% if hidden > 0 %}
        <p class="t-xs t-bold" style="margin-top: 4px">+{{ hidden }} more</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {% if notices.size > 0 %}
    <div class="notice-strip" style="padding: 6px {{ pad }}px">
      {% for notice in notices %}
        {% if notice.overflow %}
          <span class="notice notice--more">+{{ notice.overflow }}</span>
        {% else %}
          <span class="notice notice--{{ notice.level }}" title="{{ notice.text }}">
            <span class="i i-{{ notice.icon }}"></span>
          </span>
        {% endif %}
      {% endfor %}
      {% if shape.wide and notices[0].text != blank %}
        <span class="notice-said">{{ notices[0].text }}</span>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
</div>
